    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the unquestioned anchor of the lineup; his 83.29 efficiency score reflects an elite matchup against Sonny Gray, where park factors and a strong platoon advantage compensate for the starter's quality. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** also earns a high-confidence start (71.22) thanks to a favorable clash with the struggling Jose Lugo, whose 4.56 xERA provides a clear pathway for run production. Conversely, we are navigating significant volatility in the middle-to-bottom tier, as **Heliot Ramos** (63.60) benefits immensely from a soft matchup against Robbie Ray, while **Luis Lara** (59.60) remains a solid play despite the tough southpaw assignment, buoyed by an advantageous batting order position.\n\nOur most complex decision centered on the bench, where **Dominic Smith** (41.89) was the closest candidate to cracking the active roster. While his 35-PA BvP history against Zack Wheeler offered a theoretical boost, his projected efficiency failed to eclipse **Miguel Vargas** (50.01), whose ability to exploit stolen base opportunities and higher xwOBA made him the mathematically superior option for the utility spot. The roster is currently managing several constraints: **Tommy White** and **Henry Bolte** carry \"Lineup Pending\" designations, meaning their sub-50 scores are susceptible to further adjustments if they shift down the order. Furthermore, we are cautious about **Liam Hicks** (41.19), as facing Jacob deGrom suppresses his ceiling despite the platoon benefit. Keep a close eye on weather developments, as these marginal plays could dip below the floor should conditions deteriorate.",
